Subject: [PATCH 52/60] Integration fixes for fix wave 5: a merge's stray
 '=======' in styles.css (dropped UX-58's rule), one Pay by place row per
 place set (D-39), tests read the pill's sub line, data-3's department names
 and MR-28 footnote

- public/styles.css: remove a lone conflict marker left by the fix-phone-sizes merge; the rule after it
  (.d-juice.d-juice--none padding, UX-58) was dropped by the CSS parser. Never deployed.
- test/conflict-markers.test.js: npm test fails on any merge-conflict marker in a tracked source file.
- public/app.js payPlacesLine: ranges posted for the same places (Amazon's two hourly rates for Boardman,
  Hermiston and Umatilla) share one row that names the places once, each range under it (D-39).
- e2e: Beta mobile QA 3's pay-label test reads the pill and its .sal-sub line (UX-52); fix-estimates [P-10]
  accepts the longer MR-28 footnote; Fix phone controls [M-40] accepts fix-data-3's department names.

